WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.897
The interquartile range, or IQR, gives us one simple rule for flagging unusually large or small values.

00:00:08.897 --> 00:00:14.337
We calculate the first quartile, third quartile, and their difference.

00:00:14.337 --> 00:00:20.417
The upper threshold is Q3 plus one point five times the IQR.

00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:27.246
With the current values, nine hundred ninety-nine is far above the rest and should be flagged.

00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:31.015
An outlier flag is not a delete command.

00:00:31.015 --> 00:00:37.355
Unusual values may be errors, but they may also be important real observations.

00:00:37.355 --> 00:00:39.711
The next step is investigation.
